<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>PCA Visualization of the Patch Embeddings</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Visualizing the patch embeddings with PCA indicates that the spatial features contain information related to the land markers. A classifier on the patch embeddings can better detect the land markers compared to a [CLS] token-based model.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A4.F4.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:298.1pt;"><img src="2509.12146v1/img/patch_embedding/image.png" id="A4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:411/291;" width="411" height="291" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F4.fig1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A3</span>: </span><span id="A4.F4.fig1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Example multi-anatomy images with 2 images containing lead marker (top row middle and right items).</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A4.F4.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:298.1pt;"><img src="2509.12146v1/img/patch_embedding/pca_visualization.png" id="A4.F4.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:411/298;" width="411" height="298" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F4.fig2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A4</span>: </span><span id="A4.F4.fig2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">PCA visualization of the patch embeddings.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
